# Everything in this repo is consumed by Linux tooling (Docker build context,
# the container, Railway), so nothing here should ever be checked out with
# CRLF - not even on Windows. A .dockerignore with CRLF, for instance, can
# stop matching its own patterns and let .env into the build context.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The scripts run inside a Linux container: with CRLF the kernel cannot find
# the interpreter ("bad interpreter: no such file or directory").
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ini  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
